{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791690375,"nonce":"c9mbPfw1D+jt1vN2Lh2LQm8ln1A=","message":"Decision (review fix): every console holds LOCK_SH on \u003cdb_path\u003e.console.lock for its lifetime (taken in create_app before migrating, released at lifespan shutdown, O_CLOEXEC, dropped by the kernel on crash); db restore holds LOCK_EX non-blocking for the whole restore and refuses without --force while it is held; a console refuses to start while a restore holds it. The /proc checks stay as an extra. Reason: /proc cannot see a console in another PID namespace (the agent sandbox shares the data dir but not PIDs); flock works across namespaces on one kernel, like the run lock. migrate-paths is not changed: it acts on the old-layout database path, which a current console never locks.","files":null}]}